  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Four identical discs each of mass &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&#39; and diameter &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&#39; are arranged in a small plane as shown in figure. If the moment of inertia of the system about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e0a5b2da-c579-4149-aac0-7d0525226316-image.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 196px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Considering four identical discs as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5131e197-a522-4de2-8437-0c0848b698a8-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 191px;\" /></p><p>Moment of inertia of disc about diagonal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now using&nbsp;parallel axis theorem,&nbsp;</p><p>Moment of inertia of disc&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>So, net moment of inertia about&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Putting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;so,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
